{"body":{"text":["A **statement** is one sentence under the rule, saying what it conveys, the author unsure one is enough (23/116); a second is allowed only for its reason, the session's addition (23/129). A task is named as the doing (23/98), and an objection is written as what is held instead, the session's (23/119). It has no name or address, is reached by its id, and points at the utterances or sentences it rests on, shown by their numbers (23/115, 23/116)."]},"id":"1M89S32G6CZP000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Its **status** is where it stands now: open, proposed (the session's, not taken up), leaning, settled or closed (23/125, 23/137, 23/138). Each points at the utterance that gave it, so whose it is stays plain (23/129). Closed points at what closed it and may reopen on new ground; the author leans to the word, though it says nothing of why (23/138). A statement's history is its versions (23/132)."]},"id":"1M89S32G6CZP001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A **topic** is a type of its own: a short, addressable name holding statements and topics (23/86, 23/116); that a statement may stand in several is the session's (23/111). Its spans, between(session, from, to), are read from its statements' grounds and written by hand only beyond them (23/80, 23/110, 23/129)."]},"id":"1M89S32G6CZP002","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Work that belongs together is a brief in Knowledge, and its order is prose there, not typed data (23/100, 23/116). How a brief's flow holds statements is open, the session's question. Glass's values are probably to be a brief of their own, not quotes lifted one by one (23/62)."]},"id":"1M89S32G6CZP003","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Threads, paths, cycles, condensations and measures go with the redraw; until then they stay in the field and are no part of the work (23/110, 23/111). Statistics may stay (23/52)."]},"id":"1M89S32G6CZP004","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The next session starts here once the author has read and accepted it (23/138, 23/152, 23/156). It writes the types, statement and topic, with their moulds; draws the twelfth, eighteenth and twenty-third sessions, and has a blank reader read only the drawing and say what each session was, checked against the session, to see whether the elevation holds what matters (23/93, 23/129); then draws every session, gathers the work in briefs, lets the old structures go, and rewrites Knowledge whole (23/129, 23/131, 23/152). *The order the session's.*"]},"id":"1M89S32G6CZP005","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}